From 96f4ca2b75ff1cbe26770ba3fe1b3c1b3add7a39 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Tue, 6 Oct 2026 13:27:39 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Distillation review fixes: p_move in the factorised KL,
 absolute normalised gate, RNG-matched counterfactual forward

Three defects found in review of patch 0050, all in the trainer wiring (the
loss functions themselves were correct):

1. The STOP-factorised KL used stop_weight * stop_kl + move_kl, dropping the
   teacher's p_move from the move term. Steps where the teacher wants to stop
   (p_move ~ 0.05) were weighted ~10x towards imitating "where to go if not
   stopping", the opposite of the intent, and distill_stop_weight 1.0 did not
   reproduce the plain KL. Now stop_weight * stop_kl + p_move * move_kl, which
   is exactly the joint KL at weight 1.0.

2. The gate's tau <= 0 mode used the batch median JS: with 4 episodes per
   process that pushed half of every batch below exp(-1) whatever the
   absolute reachability, and the gated sum divided by total_actions halved
   the effective distillation weight. tau is now a required absolute scale
   (gate_weights refuses tau <= 0; the trainer refuses the config at start
   unless gate_min_weight is 1.0), and IL.gate_normalize (default True)
   rescales the weights to mean 1 per batch so the gate only redistributes
   the loss between steps. gate_min_weight 1.0 is a logging-only mode; the
   per-iteration JS mean and median are logged as gate_js_mean / gate_js_median
   so tau can be read off a plain-KL run (launcher: JS_LOG=True ... kl).

3. The student runs in train mode, so the own-map and counterfactual-map
   forwards drew different dropout masks and the non-map pathways did not
   cancel in the delta. The device RNG state is now captured before the
   own-map navigation forward and replayed for the counterfactual forward
   (same shapes, hence identical masks), then restored. The map encoder has
   dropout 0.0, so its once-per-rollout counterfactual tokens are exact.
   IL.effect_counterfactual "self" (own map as counterfactual) is the sanity
   check: effect_loss must be exactly 0.

Also IL.effect_reduction sum|mean (mean divides by the number of valid
candidates) for the magnitude question. Launcher: GATE_TAU required for
gated/full with the kl JS_LOG=True recipe in the error text; GATE_NORMALIZE,
EFFECT_REDUCTION, JS_LOG pass-throughs. Tests: 17.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Q37SwHSfdSLWwALjMD6Pvv
